---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { business } from '../data/business';
const quickConnectUrl = 'https://assist.zoho.com/client/syntax';
---
<Layout title="Technical Support & Remote Assistance | Syntax" description="Use the AlgaPSA client portal for ongoing support and ticket tracking, or join a technician-arranged quick remote session with Zoho Assist.">
  <section class="page-hero container">
    <p class="eyebrow"><span class="square"></span> CLIENT SUPPORT</p>
    <h1>Technical support.<br />Get back to work<span class="accent">.</span></h1>
    <div class="page-hero-bottom">
      <p>Need help or an update? Open a support ticket.<br class="desktop-break" /> Already speaking with Syntax and have a session code? Join a quick remote session.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/contact/">New project? Let’s talk <Icon name="arrow" size={19} /></a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="help-grid container" aria-label="Support options">
    <article class="help-card help-card-remote" aria-labelledby="portal-heading">
      <div class="card-top"><Icon name="strategy" size={30} /><span class="eyebrow">01 / ONGOING SUPPORT</span></div>
      <h2 id="portal-heading">Your support.<br />All in one place.</h2>
      <p>Start here for new issues, ongoing work, and ticket updates. Our AlgaPSA client portal keeps support requests and follow-up in one place for existing clients.</p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />Submit a support ticket.</li>
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />Follow updates and reply to your requests.</li>
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />Keep your support conversations together.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="help-card-action">
        <a class="button button-light" href={business.clientPortalUrl} aria-describedby="portal-status">Open support portal <Icon name="arrow" size={18} /></a>
        <p class="help-caption" id="portal-status">Need access or help signing in? <a href="/contact/">Contact Syntax</a>. Our contact form sends an email request, not an AlgaPSA ticket.</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="help-card" aria-labelledby="quick-heading">
      <div class="card-top"><Icon name="it" size={30} /><span class="eyebrow">02 / QUICK REMOTE SESSION</span></div>
      <h2 id="quick-heading">Have a session code?<br />Connect with Syntax.</h2>
      <p>Use Zoho Assist for a one-off remote session only when a Syntax technician directs you here and gives you a code. This is not a place to submit or track support tickets.</p>
      <ul class="feature-list">
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />Speak with Syntax before joining.</li>
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />Have your technician-provided session code ready.</li>
        <li><Icon name="check" size={17} />Review any download and permission prompts.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="help-card-action">
        <details class="quick-connect" id="quick-connect">
          <summary class="button button-outline">Enter session code <Icon name="plus" size={18} /></summary>
          <template id="quick-connect-template">
            <iframe id="quick-connect-frame" title="Join a Syntax remote session with Zoho Assist" width="100%" height="150" src="https://assist.zoho.com/login/embed-remote-support.jsp"></iframe>
          </template>
          <div id="quick-connect-embed"></div>
          <noscript><p class="help-caption">Use the Zoho session page linked below to enter your code.</p></noscript>
        </details>
        <p class="help-caption">Opening the code form connects your browser to Zoho Assist. If the form doesn’t load, <a href={quickConnectUrl}>open the Zoho session page</a> and choose “Join an instant remote support session,” not “Raise Your Request.” Keep ongoing requests in AlgaPSA.</p>
        <p class="help-caption">No code yet? Existing clients should <a href={business.clientPortalUrl}>open a support ticket</a>. For a first-time request, <a href="/contact/?plan=Remote%20assistance">contact Syntax</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="remote-steps-heading">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="square"></span> BEFORE WE CONNECT</p><h2 id="remote-steps-heading">Clear steps.<br />No surprise connections.</h2></div>
      <p>Zoho Assist is for quick, technician-arranged sessions. We use Level for ongoing remote support on managed devices. Neither connects automatically from this page.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="steps-grid">
      <article><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Tell us what’s wrong.</h3><p>Use the AlgaPSA portal for ongoing support, or contact Syntax for a first-time request. Include the affected device or application and how the issue affects your work. Don’t include passwords or sensitive data.</p></article>
      <article><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>We arrange the next step.</h3><p>For a quick session, we’ll provide a Zoho Assist code and guide you through joining. For managed devices, we coordinate support through Level and discuss any setup directly.</p></article>
      <article><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Connect with confidence.</h3><p>Confirm you’re speaking with Syntax before installing software or granting permissions. Keep your device online and review any approval prompt when we connect.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-section container" aria-labelledby="support-faq-heading">
    <div><p class="eyebrow"><span class="square"></span> A LITTLE MORE CLARITY</p><h2 id="support-faq-heading">Good to know.</h2></div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details><summary>Which option should I use?<Icon name="plus" size={20} /></summary><p>Use AlgaPSA to request help, discuss ongoing work, and check ticket updates. Use Zoho Assist only to join a quick remote session that a Syntax technician has arranged. Joining a Zoho session does not create an AlgaPSA ticket.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Can I join without a session code?<Icon name="plus" size={20} /></summary><p>No. Contact Syntax or open a support ticket first. A technician will coordinate the session and provide a code. The code form is not an instant-help queue and does not guarantee a technician is available.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Do I need to download anything?<Icon name="plus" size={20} /></summary><p>Zoho Assist may prompt you to download and run its remote-support app and grant permissions. Follow those steps only after confirming you’re speaking with Syntax. Ongoing managed-device support uses Level; if setup is needed, we provide instructions directly.</p></details>
      <details><summary>Where can I check my ticket status?<Icon name="plus" size={20} /></summary><p>Sign in to our <a href={business.clientPortalUrl}>AlgaPSA client portal</a> to view your support tickets, follow updates, and reply. If you need account access, contact Syntax. Requests sent through our website contact form are email inquiries and do not create portal tickets.</p></details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <aside class="help-service-note container" aria-label="Support availability">
    <span class="square"></span>
    <p>Support availability and response times follow your service agreement. Sending a request does not guarantee an immediate response or 24/7 coverage.</p>
  </aside>
</Layout>

<script>
  const quickConnect = document.querySelector<HTMLDetailsElement>('#quick-connect');
  const template = document.querySelector<HTMLTemplateElement>('#quick-connect-template');
  const embed = document.querySelector<HTMLDivElement>('#quick-connect-embed');
  if (!quickConnect || !template || !embed) {
    throw new Error('Zoho quick-connect controls are missing.');
  }
  const controls = { quickConnect, template, embed };
  quickConnect.addEventListener('toggle', () => {
    if (controls.quickConnect.open && !controls.embed.hasChildNodes()) {
      controls.embed.append(controls.template.content.cloneNode(true));
    }
  });
</script>

<style>
  .quick-connect summary { list-style: none; cursor: pointer; }
  .quick-connect summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .quick-connect[open] summary svg { transform: rotate(45deg); }
  .quick-connect iframe { display: block; margin-top: 16px; border: 0; background: #fff; }
</style>
